# behavior: a `mut` pattern binding never binds a copy: a subject reached through an index that is not a list's, such as a tuple element spelled `pair[0]`, is read out as a copy, so `Some(mut items)` on it is refused at the binding and names the shape (RFC 129 writable alias rule 8, #1846).
# expect-diagnostic: INCAN-T0126

def main() -> None:
    mut pair = (Some([1]), Some([2]))
    match pair[0]:
        Some(mut items) => items.append(3)
        None => pass
    println(pair)
